extend (wp.media, jQuery, Underscore, Backbone) is loaded by WordPress itself from
the WordPress installation, under the licences of those projects. The images in
all-in-one-favicon/images/, the files in all-in-one-favicon/styles/ and
all-in-one-favicon/scripts/, and the translation files in
all-in-one-favicon/localization/ are the original author's own work.

None of these files was modified by this fork.

SOURCE OF THE FIGURES
---------------------
The `readme.txt` shipped inside the official 4.8 ZIP and the `readme.txt` in the
plugin's own SVN trunk both declare `Tested up to: 6.2`, while the official
WordPress.org plugin API currently displays `Tested up to: 6.2.15`. Both figures are
quoted as they are, from their respective sources; this fork does not change any of
them. The plugin API reports `Requires at least: 2.8` and no `Requires PHP` value.

SECURITY REPORTS LEFT ALONE
----------------------------
In March 2023 two threads on the plugin's public support forum reported a
directory-traversal weakness ("vulnerable to Directory Traversal - critical threat",
"CRITICAL > Security Threat | Plugin abandoned?"); a third thread in January 2024
reported that the plugin produced PHP 8.2 notices. Those reports were never
answered by the author. The security question belongs to the author and is not a
compatibility question, so this fork changes no line of the code concerned; the
reports are referenced here only so that the author sees them.
